WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.262
Prudential plc is a British
multinational life insurance and

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:09.562
financial services company headquartered
in London, United Kingdom. It was

00:00:09.582 --> 00:00:14.934
founded in London in May 1848 as The
Prudential Mutual Assurance Investment

00:00:14.954 --> 00:00:20.160
and Loan Association to provide loans to
professional and working people.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:25.242
Prudential's largest division is
Prudential Corporation Asia, which has

00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:30.106
over 13 million customers across 12
Asian markets and is a top-three

00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:35.768
provider of life insurance in Hong Kong,
India, Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore,

00:00:35.788 --> 00:00:40.632
the Philippines and Vietnam. Its
Prudential UK division has around 7

00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:45.931
million customers and is a leading
provider of life insurance and pensions

00:00:45.951 --> 00:00:51.521
in the UK. Prudential also owns Jackson
National Life Insurance Company, which

00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:56.965
is one of the largest life insurance
providers in the United States, and M&amp;G

00:00:56.985 --> 00:01:01.756
Investments, a Europe-focused asset
manager with total assets under

00:01:01.776 --> 00:01:07.564
management of £547 billion at June 2014.
In December 2013 Prudential acquired the

00:01:07.584 --> 00:01:13.371
Ghanaian life insurance company, Express
Life, marking its entry into the African

00:01:13.391 --> 00:01:19.033
direct life insurance market. Prudential
subsequently rebranded the business as

00:01:19.053 --> 00:01:24.478
Prudential Ghana. In September 2014, it
purchased Kenyan life insurer Shield

00:01:24.498 --> 00:01:28.325
Assurance, rebranding the company as
Prudential Kenya.

00:01:28.345 --> 00:01:33.334
Prudential has a primary listing on the
London Stock Exchange and is a

00:01:33.354 --> 00:01:38.198
constituent of the FTSE 100 Index. It
had a market capitalisation of

00:01:38.218 --> 00:01:43.715
approximately £41,630 million as of 4
February 2015. Prudential has secondary

00:01:43.735 --> 00:01:48.651
listings on the Hong Kong Stock
Exchange, New York Stock Exchange and

00:01:48.671 --> 00:01:50.539
Singapore Exchange.
History

00:01:50.559 --> 00:01:54.386
= 1848 to 2000=
The company was founded on 30 May 1848

00:01:54.406 --> 00:01:59.540
in Hatton Garden in London as The
Prudential Mutual Assurance Investment

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:04.694
and Loan Association providing loans to
professional and working people.

00:02:04.714 --> 00:02:10.066
In 1854, the Company began selling the
relatively new concept of industrial

00:02:10.086 --> 00:02:15.801
branch insurance policies to the working
class population for premiums as low as

00:02:15.821 --> 00:02:21.318
one penny through agents acting as door
to door salesmen. The army of premium

00:02:21.338 --> 00:02:26.617
collection agents was for many years
identified with the Prudential as the

00:02:26.637 --> 00:02:30.537
"Man from the Pru".
It moved to its traditional home at

00:02:30.557 --> 00:02:36.054
Holborn Bars in 1879 and converted to a
limited company in 1881. The building

00:02:36.074 --> 00:02:41.572
was designed by Alfred Waterhouse, and
is built of terracotta manufactured by

00:02:41.592 --> 00:02:47.089
Gibbs and Canning Limited of Tamworth —
two of the same driving forces behind

00:02:47.109 --> 00:02:52.678
the Natural History Museum in London.
The Prudential Assurance Company Limited

00:02:52.698 --> 00:02:56.526
was first listed on the London Stock
Exchange in 1924.

00:02:56.546 --> 00:03:01.680
In 1986, Prudential acquired the
American insurer Jackson National Life.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:07.197
In 1997, Prudential acquired Scottish
Amicable, a business originally founded

00:03:07.217 --> 00:03:12.206
in 1826 in Glasgow as the West of
Scotland Life Insurance Company, for

00:03:12.226 --> 00:03:15.255
£1.75bn.
In 1998, Prudential set up Egg, an

00:03:15.275 --> 00:03:20.191
internet bank within the UK. The
subsidiary reached 550,000 customers

00:03:20.211 --> 00:03:25.781
within nine months but had difficulty
achieving profitability. In June 2000 an

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:31.080
initial public offering of 21% was made
to allow for further growth of the

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:36.742
internet business but in February 2006
Prudential decided to repurchase the 21%

00:03:36.762 --> 00:03:41.606
share of Egg. Egg was subsequently sold
to Citibank in January 2007.

00:03:41.626 --> 00:03:45.671
In 1999, M&amp;G, a UK fund management
company, was acquired.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:51.116
In June 2000, the Company was first
listed on the New York Stock Exchange to

00:03:51.136 --> 00:03:54.455
help focus on the US market.
= 2000 to present=

00:03:54.475 --> 00:03:59.609
In October 2004 Prudential launched a
new subsidiary, PruHealth, a joint

00:03:59.629 --> 00:04:05.416
venture with Discovery Holdings of South
Africa selling private medical insurance

00:04:05.436 --> 00:04:09.482
to the UK market.
In April 2008 Prudential outsourced its

00:04:09.502 --> 00:04:14.636
back office functions to Capita: about
3,000 jobs were transferred. This

00:04:14.656 --> 00:04:20.298
significant outsourcing deal, worth an
estimated £722m over a 15-year contract,

00:04:20.318 --> 00:04:25.234
built on Prudential's existing
relationship with Capita who took over

00:04:25.254 --> 00:04:31.042
its Belfast operation in 2006 along with
approximately 450 employees in a smaller

00:04:31.062 --> 00:04:35.470
operational restructure.
On 1 March 2010, Prudential announced

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:40.624
that it was in "advanced talks" to
purchase the pan-Asian life insurance

00:04:40.644 --> 00:04:46.286
company of AIG, American International
Assurance for approximately £23 billion.

00:04:46.306 --> 00:04:51.005
The deal later collapsed and AIA ended
up raising money in an IPO.

00:04:51.025 --> 00:04:56.377
In December 2013, Prudential announced
the purchase of Ghana’s Express Life

00:04:56.397 --> 00:05:01.603
Company. Express Life was subsequently
rebranded as Prudential Ghana. .In

00:05:01.623 --> 00:05:07.193
April, Prudential launched two corporate
responsibility initiatives to support

00:05:07.213 --> 00:05:12.492
education in Ghana: the Prudential
Scholarship Programme for more than 500

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:17.646
senior high school students, in
partnership with the NGO Plan Ghana; and

00:05:17.666 --> 00:05:21.058
a scheme to support actuarial science
graduates.

00:05:21.078 --> 00:05:26.793
In September 2014, Prudential purchased
Kenyan life insurer Shield Assurance and

00:05:26.813 --> 00:05:32.092
rebranded it as Prudential Ghana,
further expanding the company’s presence

00:05:32.112 --> 00:05:35.650
in Africa.
On 10 March 2015, it was announced that

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:40.804
the CEO, Tidjane Thiam, would leave
Prudential to become the next CEO of

00:05:40.824 --> 00:05:46.176
Credit Suisse. On 1 May 2015, it was
announced that Mike Wells, head of the

00:05:46.196 --> 00:05:51.547
company's US business, would succeed
Tidjane Thiam as CEO, on a pay package

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:54.088
worth up to £7.5 million.
Operations

00:05:54.108 --> 00:05:59.242
The Company has four business units:
Prudential UK, Europe &amp; Africa: the

00:05:59.262 --> 00:06:04.251
business offers pensions, annuities,
savings and investments. They are

00:06:04.271 --> 00:06:09.333
particularly well known for the sale of
with-profit bonds and pensions,

00:06:09.353 --> 00:06:14.414
corporate pension schemes, bulk
annuities and individual annuities. The

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:19.423
company left the general insurance
market in 2002, licensing Churchill

00:06:19.443 --> 00:06:24.650
Insurance to use the Prudential name.
M&amp;G: the business offers investment

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:29.877
management services including retail
fund management, institutional fixed

00:06:29.897 --> 00:06:35.103
income, pooled life, pension funds,
property and private finance. Part of

00:06:35.123 --> 00:06:40.403
M&amp;G, Prudential Property Investment
Managers specialises in the management

00:06:40.423 --> 00:06:45.411
of Prudential's property assets.
Prudential Corporation Asia: based in

00:06:45.431 --> 00:06:50.856
Hong Kong, the business is the largest
UK life assurer in Asia. It has had a

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:55.792
presence in the continent since 1923
when an overseas agency for life

00:06:55.812 --> 00:07:01.237
assurance was created in India. Although
this was subsequently nationalised,

00:07:01.257 --> 00:07:06.899
Prudential relaunched in India in 2000
as ICICI Prudential, a 26% joint venture

00:07:06.919 --> 00:07:12.271
with ICICI Bank. As CITIC Prudential
Life, a 50–50 joint venture, they were

00:07:12.291 --> 00:07:17.570
the first UK company to re-establish
life business in China in 2000. There

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:22.724
are also businesses in Hong Kong,
Taiwan, Japan, South Korea, Singapore,

00:07:22.744 --> 00:07:28.169
Malaysia, Philippines, Thailand, Vietnam
and Indonesia. On 15 November 2011,

00:07:28.189 --> 00:07:33.686
Prudential Corporation Asia announced
its intention to change the name of its

00:07:33.706 --> 00:07:37.388
asset management business to Eastspring
Investments.

00:07:37.408 --> 00:07:42.978
Jackson National Life Insurance Company:
based in Michigan, United States, the

00:07:42.998 --> 00:07:48.567
business was purchased in 1986. It was
named after Andrew Jackson, the seventh

00:07:48.587 --> 00:07:53.649
President of the United States of
America and started business in 1961.

00:07:53.669 --> 00:07:57.641
Prudential RideLondon
Prudential RideLondon is an annual

00:07:57.661 --> 00:08:03.376
two-day cycling festival that started in
2013. The third edition will take place

00:08:03.396 --> 00:08:06.643
on Saturday 1 August and Sunday 2 August
2015.

00:08:06.663 --> 00:08:12.378
The event was developed by the Mayor of
London and his agencies and is organised

00:08:12.398 --> 00:08:16.951
by the London &amp; Surrey Cycling
Partnership.. The main events are

00:08:16.971 --> 00:08:22.613
a100-mile professional road race through
Surrey and London, and an amateur race

00:08:22.633 --> 00:08:28.058
along the same route. Participants in
the amateur race typically raise money

00:08:28.078 --> 00:08:33.502
for good causes. The 20,709 finishers in
the 2014 event raised more than £10

00:08:33.522 --> 00:08:36.697
million for charity.
Swansea Bay Tidal Lagoon

00:08:36.717 --> 00:08:42.141
In October 2014, Prudential announced
that it will invest up to £100 million

00:08:42.161 --> 00:08:47.658
in the Swansea Bay Tidal Lagoon Power
station, a world-leading infrastructure

00:08:47.678 --> 00:08:53.103
project. Prudential has committed to
invest £25 billion in UK infrastructure

00:08:53.123 --> 00:08:58.620
projects over five years. Prudential
will be one of the main investors in the

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:04.354
scheme designed to harness tidal-energy,
which could power 120,000 homes for 120

00:09:04.374 --> 00:09:07.621
years.
If approved, the project would take two

00:09:07.641 --> 00:09:11.614
years to build and would create 1,850
construction jobs.

